Let this platform use the struct statfs f_type arm.

fcstat.c walks a chain of arms to work out a filesystem's type from fstatfs(),
and ends in "#error BUG: No way to figure out with fstatfs()" when none matches.
Nothing matched here: the f_fstypename arm is for the BSDs, and the f_type arm
is gated on __linux__, which this build deliberately undefines.

The f_type arm is nevertheless exactly right for this system.  Its struct statfs
has f_type, and the kernel fills it with the same filesystem magic numbers the
arm switches on -- 0x4d44 for FAT (so fontconfig knows that filesystem's mtime
granularity is too coarse to trust for cache validity) and the ext4 magic
otherwise.  So this adds the platform to the arm rather than writing a new one.

--- a/src/fcstat.c
+++ b/src/fcstat.c
@@ -386,7 +386,7 @@
 #  endif
 #  if defined(HAVE_STRUCT_STATFS_F_FSTYPENAME)
 	p = buf.f_fstypename;
-#  elif defined(__linux__) || defined (__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#  elif defined(__linux__) || defined (__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__LIKEOS__)
 	switch (buf.f_type)
 	{
 	case 0x6969: /* nfs */
